          "message": "Rename allocation info function for consistency (#5)\n\nMaking the function name consistency across rust and elixir makes usage\r\nfrom other libraries or services much easier after the rustler 0.22\r\nupgrade, which makes it harder to re-export other rust nifs under\r\ndifferent names (i.e., it's easier to export\r\n`jemalloc_info::jemalloc_allocation_info` in the rustler init than\r\n`jemalloc_info::allocation_info as foo`).",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "08f65c36fca2de6a817ada0e1c8743941bc310e6",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/jemalloc_info/git/trees/08f65c36fca2de6a817ada0e1c8743941bc310e6"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/jemalloc_info/git/commits/9c7d68de2014e9948a3344087f3421a33e78916f",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJhAFM1CRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAA5DQIAK8i6uw+DyZ59shbkoWMs2tn\nAIZH0VQpS6HnsBgQ8mZPUilQGCj5pUrJwhQ/vVD3Da1ydPa8ibQbYYZC3ZnssqUo\nwXR32vyXfcQp6PvVo5nIrDmHfrgPy4/UzwhwKKAShxeUQqPL9OAzlt1hGo3kTHzu\nNWeW0tnFQCfFmdFpgl6vbssDgOklSOSbotDtIUAvgF0E8AjfHc4r8+kvAyKX8Mus\nbkt9I447eBY6qQoUH0VkhRJhFl1bUyn8MqOCOxR16x86pr/5safwPiYvtnIHkz0q\nE1sDqjH4AOwUocNWqT8mPprkmvep+8c3i3cVSQgMkOS1saI0737s38jTHxB0CL4=\n=7akg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree 08f65c36fca2de6a817ada0e1c8743941bc310e6\nparent c9cc7fec0e90f2eed082d84e0e138f07d10fa762\nauthor Isobel Redelmeier <iredelmeier@gmail.com> 1627411253 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1627411253 -0700\n\nRename allocation info function for consistency (#5)\n\nMaking the function name consistency across rust and elixir makes usage\r\nfrom other libraries or services much easier after the rustler 0.22\r\nupgrade, which makes it harder to re-export other rust nifs under\r\ndifferent names (i.e., it's easier to export\r\n`jemalloc_info::jemalloc_allocation_info` in the rustler init than\r\n`jemalloc_info::allocation_info as foo`)."
          }
